  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "John Wayne Mallo was an American businessman who built a regional car-rental enterprise from an Akron Budget franchise opened in 1967. A Kent State graduate, he expanded into Arizona, Columbus and Las Vegas, buying and selling local licences. His family’s automotive businesses later included car dealerships and the Splash Car Wash chain.",
    "confidence": {
      "score": 91,
      "band": "high",
      "reason": "Trade and family records corroborate identity, education and regional business expansion."
    },
    "source_ids": [
      "S1",
      "S2"
    ],
    "word_count": 52,
    "html": "<p>John Wayne Mallo was an American businessman who built a regional car-rental enterprise from an Akron Budget franchise opened in 1967. A Kent State graduate, he expanded into Arizona, Columbus and Las Vegas, buying and selling local licences. His family’s automotive businesses later included car dealerships and the Splash Car Wash chain.</p>\r\n"
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "John Mallo turned fleet ownership into a second line of business. As a Budget operator, he bought vehicles outright rather than relying entirely on manufacturers’ guaranteed depreciation programmes, and became an early franchisee to establish a dedicated used-car sales operation. He also enlisted basketball player Steve Kerr for a local advertising campaign.\n\nWhen his family diversified into car washing, the physical experience mattered. At Splash, they chose a longer wash tunnel and a curved, translucent roof to make the building brighter and more open. His son Joe returned from Las Vegas to join the venture in 2016, with further generations later working in marketing and site management.",
    "confidence": {
      "score": 87,
      "band": "high",
      "reason": "Trade recollections establish purchasing, resale and advertising; the contemporary family profile documents design choices and family participation."
    },
    "source_ids": [
      "S2",
      "S3",
      "S4"
    ],
    "word_count": 107,
    "html": "<p>John Mallo turned fleet ownership into a second line of business. As a Budget operator, he bought vehicles outright rather than relying entirely on manufacturers’ guaranteed depreciation programmes, and became an early franchisee to establish a dedicated used-car sales operation. He also enlisted basketball player Steve Kerr for a local advertising campaign.</p>\r\n<p>When his family diversified into car washing, the physical experience mattered. At Splash, they chose a longer wash tunnel and a curved, translucent roof to make the building brighter and more open. His son Joe returned from Las Vegas to join the venture in 2016, with further generations later working in marketing and site management.</p>\r\n"
  },
